From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 21:05:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] One Scripture reference parser for the site and the scripts
 (U09)

client/src/lib/scripture-ref.ts is the site's one reader of references
("John 3:16", "jn 3 16", "1 cor 13", "Romans 13", "Ps 23:1-3",
"Philippians 4:6-7"; null for an unknown book or a chapter or verse that
cannot exist). It is built from scripts/lib/bsb.mjs's logic, extended with
the abbreviations people write, loose spacing, "." between chapter and
verse, chapters joined by semicolons, and one-chapter books cited by verse
("Jude 3"). The book table and abbreviations live once, in
client/src/data/scripture-books.json, which both runtimes read.

scripts/lib/bsb.mjs gets readRef, the same grammar line for line (parseRef
now wraps it and still throws), and finds its root with fileURLToPath so
Vite-run tests can import it. scripture-ref.test.ts runs both parsers on one
fixture list and on every reference in the Study Bible's guides, doctrine
studies, and Find Help pages, and fails on any disagreement; it also holds
the book table to /bible/books.json and each alias to one book.

Retired onto it: refHref in lib/bible-notes.ts (doctrine key texts, guide
"Read:" lines, verse notes), studyBibleHref in lib/needs.ts (care pages'
"Read the whole chapter"), and refChapters' own alias table (related
content on Study Bible chapters). The books argument those needed is gone,
and the guides page no longer fetches books.json. The OSIS parser in
lib/bible.ts stays for the Study Bible's internal codes.

Checked against the old code on every reference string the site's data
feeds these functions: 13,772 give the same link or chapters; 6 differ, all
catalogue lines that now resolve (Jude 3, Philemon 15-16) or no longer
borrow a chapter from another book. The bsb-based validators print
byte-identical output, and the 441 references they read name the same
verses.

